
I've been bored with the normal sestina forms so i decided to take it a bit extreme, 

Constraint Name: Doustina

Requirements:

Stanzas: 6

Lines per stanza: 6

Total lines: 36

Rotating words per line: 2 (1 endword like a traditional sestina + 1 internal rotating word)

Total rotating words: 12 (6 sets × 2 words)

Rotation pattern is like a sestina (6→1→5→2→4→3) also morphological variants are permitted (Eg: writing "bend" as "bent" etc..)

Endword rule:

second rotating word in each rotation set must appear as the final word of the corresponding line (endword)

Envoi:

Compulsory, consisting of 2 stanzas of 3 lines each, 2 of the rotating words must be the line embedded too, 6 lines - 12/12 rotating words

Tristina is the same thing but with 3 rotating words per line and its Envoi has 3 stanzas, Quastina is 4 rotating words per line with a 4 stanza Envoi

