And now the Final Boss, A StrayQuastina here are

two poems from an ongoing series built around an experimental form I created called the "StrayQuastina", an extreme variation of the Quastina

Constraint Name: StrayQuastina (Extreme variation of the Quastina), 

StrayQuastina Requirements:

Stanzas: 6

Lines per stanza: 6

Total lines: 36

Rotating words per line: 4 (1 endword  like a traditional sestina + 3 internal rotating words)

Total rotating words: 24 (6 sets × 4 words)

Rotation pattern is like a sestina (6→1→5→2→4→3) also morphological variants are permitted. (Eg: writing "bend" as "bent" etc..)

Endword rule:

fourth rotating word in each rotation set must appear as the final word of the corresponding line (endword)

Internal order:

 The 4 rotating words must appear in fixed sequence within each line

Thematic requirement:

 Each of the 6 stanzas must have a distinct theme and tell different things mostly with different phrasing 

Word cap:

 Must be ≤8 words per line

Ban Rule: No rotating word should be reused across multiple StrayQuastinas (Part Of A Series)

Envoi: A StrayQuastina variant usually doesn't come with an Envoi, it's optional

Rotating word sets: 

cold - form - bend - edges

silent - fields - hold - motion

empty - frame - shift - depth

loose - pattern - drift - center

faint - trace - pull - distance

still - axis - mark - change

